  "core": "Fulfillment arrives when what was desired meets what is present — the moment the two stop being separate. In Imagination, that meeting happens in the space where images form: the picture held in the mind touches the thing actually there, and they recognize each other. When this collision stays invisible, the satisfaction arrives but finds no name, no marking, no one standing witness to the arrival. The feast is eaten in darkness.",
  "sheetLine": "The feast arrives unnamed; satisfaction has no one to tell."
